# credential_reactivated email — task ISA

> Task ISA operating against the AccessBuddy project ISA at `~/Documents/workspace/projects/accessbuddy/ISA.md`. Decisions and changelog reconcile back there at LEARN.

## Problem

When an expired fob is reactivated (confirm-programming promotes a staged renewal expiry), the member hears nothing. Their last system email said "your fob has expired" and promised automatic reactivation, but no reactivation email exists anywhere in v1.16.0. Reactivations since 1 September 2026 (season rollover) have already happened silently.

## Vision

A member whose fob was expired opens their inbox and sees "Your fob is active again" the moment the programmer confirms, closing the loop the expired email opened. Admins see that email in the credential's access log alongside the status change. Every member reactivated since 1 September gets the same email once, retrospectively, without anyone being emailed twice.

## Out of Scope

- Emailing on the admin manual-edit path (`credentials/[id]/route.ts` status → active). Nick asked for confirm-programming only.
- Reactivating expired fobs in force-renew (separate gap, noted in the earlier finding).
- Tenant-level enable/disable enforcement at send time (the registry is admin-facing today; sends key off templateType).
- Deploying or running the backfill before Nick approves the wording.

## Constraints

- `setEmailBranding()` runs before any template render (already inside `renderTemplate`).
- Inline send inside the confirm-programming transaction, audited against the CREDENTIAL entity so it lands in the access log (matches `credentialIssued` pattern).
- Backfill must respect Resend's daily cap: enqueue via `email_queue`, drained by the daily cron under budget; never send inline in bulk.
- Backfill dry-run by default, `--apply` to write, idempotent via window dedupe on entity + templateType.
- `audit_log` is FORCE RLS: backfill queries run inside a per-tenant `set_config` transaction.
- bun only. Conventional `feat:` commit on a feature branch; no merge to main until wording approved.

## Goal

`credential_reactivated` exists in the registry and template set, fires inline from confirm-programming's reactivate branch with an `email_sent` audit entry on the credential, and a dry-run-first backfill script enqueues the same email for every expired→active reactivation since 2026-09-01 without duplicates. Wording presented to Nick for sign-off before merge.

