## Decisions

- 2026-09-04: Task ISA rather than editing the E4 project ISA directly; reconcile a Decision + Changelog into the project ISA at LEARN.
- 2026-09-04: Backfill enqueues rather than sends inline, so Resend's 100/day cap and the cron's dedupe protect it. Cost: delivery waits for the next daily cron run.
- 2026-09-04: Only confirm-programming wired (Nick's explicit scope). Admin manual edit left unwired and noted.
- 2026-09-04: Advisor (Inference.ts) flagged: tx-shared audit connection, audit row shape, reply-to promise, immediacy wording. Verified first two by reading `writeEmailAudit` (uses `audit.tx`) and confirm-programming's `STATUS_CHANGE expired→active` audit; kept "just reply to this email" because the expired email already uses it and `replyToEmail` is tenant-configured; dropped immediacy language so a late backfill send still reads true.
- 2026-09-04: Advisor's suggestion to enqueue on inline failure not adopted. Every other transactional send in the codebase is inline-only with email_failed audit; adding a fallback for one template would be inconsistent. Noted as a possible platform-wide improvement.
- 2026-09-04: Backfill also catches admin_edit reactivations (same audit shape). Nick asked for "any activations since the first of September", so the wider net is correct; dry-run output shows the source per row.
- 2026-09-04: Delegation floor (E3 ≥2) relaxed, show-your-math: two-file surgical edits plus one script in a live prod product where Nick has a pending wording gate. Forge/Anvil would add a second author to code I must present line-by-line; accessbuddy-qa-verify cannot probe prod without the IP toggle Nick has not authorised this session. Reviewer pass done via Advisor instead.

